---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Imprint from '../components/Imprint.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../lib/company';
import { PLANS } from '../lib/plans';
import { SESSION_COOKIE } from '../lib/auth';

const user = Astro.locals.user;

/** Fixed on purpose — see the note in terms.astro. */
const updated = '11 August 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy">
  <div class="page">
    <SiteHeader user={user} />

    <div class="wrap prose-wrap stack gap-20" style="padding-block: 48px 64px">
      <header>
        <h1 class="h2">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top: 8px">
          What Easy Screen Capture collects, why, where it goes and how long it stays. Last updated {updated}.
        </p>
      </header>

      <Imprint heading="Who is responsible" />
      <p class="small muted" style="margin-top: -12px">
        {COMPANY.name} is the controller for the personal data described here. For anything about your data, write to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>. We have not appointed a data protection officer; the
        scale of processing does not require one.
      </p>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="stack gap-6 small muted">
          <li>· <b>Account:</b> your email address, display name, and a PBKDF2 hash of your password. We never store the password itself.</li>
          <li>· <b>Sessions:</b> a SHA-256 hash of the session cookie, its creation and expiry time, and the browser's user-agent string.</li>
          <li>· <b>API keys:</b> a SHA-256 hash of each key with its visible prefix and last four characters, a label, and when it was last used. The key itself is shown once and never stored.</li>
          <li>· <b>Captures:</b> the URL and host you captured, the device, viewport, mode and format, status, duration, byte size, and the rendered image or PDF files.</li>
          <li>· <b>Usage:</b> a monthly counter of captures made through the app and through the API, and short-lived per-minute rate-limit counters.</li>
          <li>· <b>Billing:</b> if you subscribe, your Stripe customer and subscription identifiers, plan, status, billing interval and paid-through date. Card details go to Stripe directly and never reach our servers.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted">
          We do not run analytics, advertising or third-party trackers, and we do not build profiles or make automated
          decisions with legal effect. Cloudflare, which serves the site, keeps standard request logs including IP
          addresses for its own security purposes; we do not keep our own access logs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
        <div class="deflist">
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Run your account and take captures</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Confirm your email address</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Performance of the contract</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Take payment and issue invoices</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Contract, and legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c))</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Keep accounting and tax records</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Legal obligation</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Enforce quotas, prevent abuse, keep the service secure</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f))</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Service emails about your account</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Contract</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted">
          Providing your email and password is necessary to have an account — without them the service cannot be
          supplied.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">Pages you capture</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          A capture is a picture of someone else's page, so it may contain personal data of other people. For that
          content you are the controller and we act on your instructions as processor: we render it, store it and
          serve it back to you, and nothing else. Do not capture pages behind a login or containing special-category
          data unless you are entitled to.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          Every capture carries a share token embedded in its file links. Anyone who holds a link can open that
          capture's files without signing in, so treat links as you would the files themselves. Deleting a capture
          removes the stored files and invalidates its links.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">How long we keep it</h2>
        <div class="deflist">
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Captures and their files</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">
              {PLANS.free.historyDays} days ({PLANS.free.name}) · {PLANS.plus.historyDays} days ({PLANS.plus.name} and
              {' '}{PLANS.pro.name}) · {PLANS.business.historyDays} days ({PLANS.business.name})
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Sessions</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Until expiry or sign-out</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Email confirmation tokens</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Until used or expired</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Rate-limit counters</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Minutes — they expire by themselves</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Account and usage records</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">While the account exists</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Invoices and accounting records</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">As Bulgarian law requires, currently 10 years</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted">
          A nightly job deletes captures past their plan's retention window, files included. Deleting your account
          removes your captures, sessions and API keys with it; billing records that we are obliged to keep remain in
          Stripe and in our accounts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">Who processes it for us</h2>
        <div class="deflist">
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Cloudflare, Inc.</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Hosting, database, file storage and page rendering</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Stripe, Inc. / Stripe Payments Europe</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Payments, subscriptions, invoices and tax</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <span class="deflist__label">Resend, Inc.</span>
            <span class="deflist__value">Sending account emails</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted">
          Each is bound by a data processing agreement. They are US companies and processing may take place outside
          the EEA; those transfers rely on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and, where the provider is certified,
          the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. We do not sell your data or share it for anyone else's marketing. We
          disclose data to authorities only where the law requires it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          One cookie, <span class="mono">{SESSION_COOKIE}</span>, keeps you signed in. It is strictly necessary,
          HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite=Lax, and it is removed when you sign out. There are no analytics or
          advertising cookies, which is why the site does not ask for cookie consent. The app also stores a small
          offline cache in your browser so it works without a connection; you can clear it from your browser
          settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          You can ask for access to your data, correction, erasure, restriction, portability, and you can object to
          processing based on legitimate interests. Most of it is in your hands already: edit your profile, delete any
          capture, revoke any API key, and delete the whole account — all from the account screen, with no need to ask
          us. For anything else, write to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> — we answer within 30
          days.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          If you think we have handled your data wrongly you may complain to the {COMPANY.dpa.name}, the Bulgarian
          supervisory authority (<a href={COMPANY.dpa.url} rel="noopener">{COMPANY.dpa.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>),
          or to the authority where you live.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">Changes</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          We will update this policy as the service changes and revise the date above. If a change materially affects
          you, we will tell you by email.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Base>
